tion":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nOnly tried in 4.5.dev2.official.af2c71397; not going to worry about this being a regression because it just prints a spurious warning so it's not high priority to fix.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev2 - Debian GNU/Linux trixie/sid trixie on Wayland - X11 display driver, Single-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (RPL-P) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-1360P (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nA singleton added from a GDExtension:\n\n- Does not have instance methods/properties available from just its name in GDScript (it acts like any other class).\n- Still gives warnings as if it did.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Call a method on a GDExtension singleton from GDScript.\n2. Run the project.\n3. ```log\n   WARNING:   The function \"say_cheese()\" is a static function but was called from an instance. Instead, it should be directly called from the type: \"MySingleton.say_cheese()\".\n   ```\n\nBut if you follow that suggestion:\n\n```log\nERROR: Cannot call non-static function \"say_cheese()\" on the class \"MySingleton\" directly. Make an instance instead.\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nhttps://github.com/BenLubar/godot-cpp-singleton-repro/commit/c01235e6ac181eae24a32c0903a6be53157debce\n\n(Not attaching a zip file of this because it would have to contain the entirety of godot-cpp to be usable.)","closed_by":{"login":"BenLubar","id":4257305,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNTczMDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4257305?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BenLubar","html_url":"https://github.com/BenLubar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BenLubar/followers","follow